ion is to keep monthly recurring revenue at or above £126,000 / month: I need a size for the links from Support capacity strain to monthly recurring revenue, from Price rise to Price-rise churn and from Starter tier support cost to Support capacity strain. Roughly how much monthly recurring revenue in £/month does a change in Support capacity strain bring?\n\nThis model doesn't yet say whether any option gets there within 9 months.\n\nThe model was saved. Questions this model does not answer yet: Does \"monthly recurring revenue\" get there within 9 months? The model holds the deadline; no result answers that yet. \"monthly recurring revenue\" depends on \"Starter tier support cost\", which is \"Starter tier subscribers\" times \"Support cost per starter subscriber\". Olumi's analysis multiplies them when every part has a figure and together they match \"Starter tier support cost\" (within 5%); otherwise Olumi will ask you which figure is right before it analyses. (2 of 6 shown.)"},{"turn_id":"d9eea73b-3dac-487e-98e6-e9416d056217","created_at":"2026-10-07T02:36:21.073143+00:00","user_message":"Run analysis","assistant_message":"Your results are ready. You can view them now or ask me to explain them.\n\nThis run doesn’t show how often each option reaches the goal’s target. I can't yet say how likely any option is to keep monthly recurring revenue at or above £126,000 / month: I need a size for the links from Support capacity strain to monthly recurring revenue, from Price rise to Price-rise churn and from Starter tier support cost to Support capacity strain.\n\nThis model doesn't yet say whether any option gets there within 9 months."},{"turn_id":"c69bb5f4-3fd3-4d48-af5e-ac0f970aa2b2","created_at":"2026-10-07T02:36:30.881141+00:00","user_message":"Explain this result","assistant_message":"No option can be put forward from this run: important relationships remain unsized.\n\nThis run doesn’t show how often each option reaches the goal’s target. I can't yet say how lik